A note on responsible use
-------------------------
These are survey and phishing-simulation records from staff at a single
university, collected under an approved ethics protocol and linked by hashed
identifiers so that neither the researchers nor the institution's IT security
team could see identifiable survey responses.

Direct identifiers have been removed and free-text fields screened. Even so,
because the population is one institution, combinations of banded age, gender
and role should be treated as potentially identifying. Do not attempt to
re-identify participants, and do not link these records to other datasets in
a way that would make re-identification possible.
